  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88f6fa2b89436164b8e97b17d82dc9a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 5 - Data Types
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_data_types
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Data Types
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: "Data types define the kind of value used in the program.\r\nDifferent
    data types are used for different kinds of information such as numbers, text,
    or logical values.\r\n\r\nExamples of common data types:\r\n<indent=2em>- <font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#4FC3F7>int</color></font> (Integer) \u2192 whole numbers \u2192
    <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#B5CEA8>10</color>, <color=#B5CEA8>-3</color>,
    <color=#B5CEA8>42</color></font></indent>\r\n<indent=2em>- <font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#4FC3F7>float</color></font> (Float) \u2192 decimal numbers \u2192
    <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#B5CEA8>2.5</color>, <color=#B5CEA8>0.75</color>,
    <color=#B5CEA8>-1.0</color></font></indent>\r\n<indent=2em>- <font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#4FC3F7>str</color></font> (String) \u2192 text values \u2192 <font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#CE9178>\"wall\"</color>, <color=#CE9178>\"robot\"</color>, <color=#CE9178>\"hello\"</color></font></indent>\r\n<indent=2em>-
    <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#4FC3F7>bool</color></font> (Boolean) \u2192
    true or false values \u2192 <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>True</color>,
    <color=#55AAFF>False</color></font></indent>\r\n\r\nUsing the correct data type
    is important because different operations and commands may only work with specific
    types of data."
  isImageBig: 0
